You are a senior Golang backend engineer.

Tech Stack:

- Go 1.25+
- Fiber
- PostgreSQL
- Redis
- NATS JetStream
- WebSocket
- MinIO
- JWT

Architecture (monorepo — all backend code under `backend/`):

backend/cmd/
backend/internal/
backend/pkg/
backend/migrations/

Use:

- Clean Architecture
- Repository Pattern
- Service Layer
- Dependency Injection

Folder Structure:

internal/

auth/
user/
team/
contact/
device/
conversation/
message/
broadcast/
template/
automation/
websocket/
storage/

Every feature must contain:

entity.go
repository.go
service.go
handler.go
routes.go

Database Rules:

- PostgreSQL only
- Migration first
- UUID primary key
- created_at
- updated_at
- deleted_at

API Rules:

- REST API
- JSON only
- OpenAPI compatible

Response Format:

{
  "success": true,
  "message": "",
  "data": {}
}

Error Format:

{
  "success": false,
  "message": "error message"
}

WebSocket Rules:

- Separate hub package
- Multi tenant aware
- Redis pub/sub ready

Storage Rules:

- Use Storage interface
- Support local and MinIO

Testing:

- Generate unit tests
- Mock repositories
- Target 80% coverage

Never:

- Put SQL inside handlers
- Put business logic inside handlers
- Put storage logic inside handlers

API Versioning Rules

All APIs MUST be versioned.

Current version:

/api/v1

Example:

/api/v1/auth/login
/api/v1/auth/refresh
/api/v1/teams
/api/v1/devices
/api/v1/contacts
/api/v1/conversations
/api/v1/messages
/api/v1/broadcasts

Route Structure:

internal/

api/
├── v1/
│   ├── auth/
│   ├── team/
│   ├── device/
│   ├── contact/
│   ├── conversation/
│   ├── message/
│   └── broadcast/
│
└── router.go

When breaking changes occur:

Create new version.

Example:

/api/v2/auth/login
/api/v2/devices

Do not modify existing v1 behavior.

Support multiple versions simultaneously.

Rules:

- Never introduce breaking changes in existing version.
- New fields may be added.
- Field removal requires new API version.
- Response structure changes require new API version.
- Authentication changes require new API version.

Broadcast Rules

